**Sr DevOps**

We are seeking a Senior DevOps Engineer for our team to ensure that we continue to provide all patients with high quality, efficient care. Did you get into our industry for these reasons? We are an amazing team that works hard to support each other and are seeking a phenomenal addition like you who feels patient care is as meaningful as we do. We want you to apply!

**Job Summary and Qualifications**

The DevOps Engineer delivers on strategic commitments from start to finish for all aspects of the Clinical Services Group organization within ITG. This position is responsible for supporting day-to-day operation of  critical infrastructure that allows our providers to deliver the best care possible to patients across the enterprise. An ideal candidate can quickly learn and make use of existing solutions as well as research and implement new technologies based on identified areas for improvement. They understand the services provided while understanding the direction of the Clinical Services Group. Additionally, they can develop strong relationships throughout the organization to assist in accomplishing its goals for the company.

Previous job titles like SRE, DevOps Engineer, or Software Engineer might make you a good fit for this position.

The DevOps Engineer works with development teams to support current environments, infrastructure automation, and software deployment. They will provide problem resolutions for systems as needed.

In addition the candidate should possess  analysis and design ability, creativity for problem solving, troubleshooting and innovation ability; knowledge of the business implications of technical approaches, directions, and solutions; ability to innovate in complex technical areas, ability to achieve results, project planning/coordination skills, and strong communication skills.

**GENERAL RESPONSIBILITIES**

Responsibilities:

- Build tools, automations, and infrastructure that enable teams that rely on SysOps to be successful with minimal interaction and manual intervention from team members
- Write code to automate operations in Python and Ansible
- Run our infrastructure with Ansible , Terraform, Python, PowerShell, Bash, etc. in a hybrid public cloud (Azure and GCP) and on-premises environments.
- Design and implement custom 24x7 monitoring and alerting solutions
- Research, investigate, and implement new technologies
- Build monitoring that alerts of symptoms rather than on outages to stop issues before they happen
- Be on an on-call rotation to respond to incidents that impact critical processes that may impact patient care or financials

 

